  "csp.5.R.RH.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of primary and secondary sources, attending to such features as the date and origin of the information."];
  "csp.RH.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of primary and secondary sources."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or information of a primary or secondary source; provide an accurate summary of how key events or ideas develop over the course of the text."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or information of a primary or secondary source; provide an accurate summary of the source distinct from prior knowledge or opinions."];
  "csp.9.12.3.3" [label="Analyze in detail a series of events described in a text; determine whether earlier events caused later ones or simply preceded them."];
  "csp.RH.3" [label="Identify key steps in a text's description of a process related to history/social studies (e.g., how a bill becomes law, how interest rates are raised or lowered)."];
  "csp.6.R.RH.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of primary and secondary sources, connecting insights gained from specific details to an understanding of the text as a whole."];
  "csp.11.12.2.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or information of a primary or secondary source; provide an accurate summary that makes clear the relationships among the key details and ideas."];
  "csp.6.R.RH.4" [label="Evaluate various explanations for actions or events and determine which explanation best accords with textual evidence, acknowledging where the text leaves matters uncertain."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.4" [label="Determine the meaning of words and phrases as they are used in a text, including vocabulary describing political, social, or economic aspects of history/social studies."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.4" [label="Determine the meaning of words and phrases as they are used in a text, including vocabulary specific to domains related to history/social studies."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.5" [label="Analyze how a text uses structure to emphasize key points or advance an explanation or analysis."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.5" [label="Describe how a text presents information (e.g., sequentially, comparatively, causally)."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.6" [label="Compare the point of view of two or more authors for how they treat the same or similar topics, including which details they include and emphasize in their respective accounts."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.6" [label="Identify aspects of a text that reveal an author's point of view or purpose (e.g., loaded language, inclusion or avoidance of particular facts)."];
  "opensalt.4." [label="Determine the meaning of words and phrases as they are used in a text, including analyzing how an author uses and refines the meaning of a key term over the course of a text (e.g., how Madison defines faction in *Federalist* No. 10)."];
  "opensalt.5." [label="Analyze in detail how a complex primary source is structured, including how key sentences, paragraphs, and larger portions of the text contribute to the whole."];
  "csp.6.R.RH.7" [label="Evaluate authors' differing points of view on the same historical event or issue by assessing the authors' claims, reasoning, and evidence."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.7" [label="Integrate quantitative or technical analysis (e.g., charts, research data) with qualitative analysis in print or digital text."];
  "csp.RH.7" [label="Integrate visual information (e.g., in charts, graphs, photographs, videos, or maps) with other information in print and digital texts."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.8" [label="Assess the extent to which the reasoning and evidence in a text support the author's claims."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.8" [label="Distinguish among fact, opinion, and reasoned judgment in a text."];
  "csp.5.R.RH.9" [label="Compare and contrast treatments of the same topic in several primary and secondary sources."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.9" [label="Analyze the relationship between a primary and secondary source on the same topic."];
  "opensalt.7." [label="Integrate and evaluate multiple sources of information presented in diverse formats and media (e.g., visually, quantitatively, as well as in words) in order to address a question or solve a problem."];
  "csp.6.R.RH.11" [label="Evaluate an author's premises, claims, and evidence by corroborating or challenging them with other information."];
  "csp.6.R.RH.12" [label="Integrate information from diverse sources, both primary and secondary, into a coherent understanding of an idea or event, noting discrepancies among sources."];
  "csp.RH.9-10.10" [label="By the end of grade 10, read and comprehend history/social studies texts in the grades 9—10 text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "csp.RH.6-8.10" [label="By the end of grade 8, read and comprehend history/social studies texts in the grades 6—8 text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "opensalt.10." [label="By the end of Grade 12, read and comprehend history/social studies texts in the Grades 11-CCR text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of science and technical texts, attending to the precise details of explanations or descriptions."];
  "csp.4.R.RS.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of science and technical texts."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or conclusions of a text; trace the text's explanation or depiction of a complex process, phenomenon, or concept; provide an accurate summary of the text."];
  "csp.4.R.RS.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or conclusions of a text; provide an accurate summary of the text distinct from prior knowledge or opinions."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.3" [label="Follow precisely a complex multistep procedure when carrying out experiments, taking measurements, or performing technical tasks, attending to special cases or exceptions defined in the text."];
  "csp.RST.6-8.3" [label="Follow precisely a multistep procedure when carrying out experiments, taking measurements, or performing technical tasks."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.1" [label="Cite specific textual evidence to support analysis of science and technical texts, attending to important distinctions the author makes and to any gaps or inconsistencies in the account."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.2" [label="Determine the central ideas or conclusions of a text; summarize complex concepts, processes, or information presented in a text by paraphrasing them in simpler but still accurate terms."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.3" [label="Follow precisely a complex multistep procedure when carrying out experiments, taking measurements, or performing technical tasks; analyze the specific results based on explanations in the text."];
  "csp.RST.9-10.4" [label="Determine the meaning of symbols, key terms, and other domain-specific words and phrases as they are used in a specific scientific or technical context relevant to grades 9—10 texts and topics."];
  "csp.RST.6-8.4" [label="Determine the meaning of symbols, key terms, and other domain-specific words and phrases as they are used in a specific scientific or technical context relevant to grades 6—8 texts and topics."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.5" [label="Analyze the structure of the relationships among concepts in a text, including relationships among key terms (e.g., force, friction, reaction force, energy)."];
  "csp.RST.5" [label="Analyze the structure an author uses to organize a text, including how the major sections contribute to the whole and to an understanding of the topic."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.6" [label="Analyze the author's purpose in providing an explanation, describing a procedure, or discussing an experiment in a text, defining the question the author seeks to address."];
  "csp.4.R.RS.6" [label="Analyze the author's purpose in providing an explanation, describing a procedure, or discussing an experiment in a text."];
  "csp.RST.11-12.4" [label="Determine the meaning of symbols, key terms, and other domain-specific words and phrases as they are used in a specific scientific or technical context relevant to grades 11—12 texts and topics."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.5" [label="Analyze how the text structures information or ideas into categories or hierarchies, demonstrating understanding of the information or ideas."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.6" [label="Analyze the author's purpose in providing an explanation, describing a procedure, or discussing an experiment in a text, identifying important issues that remain unresolved."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.7" [label="Translate quantitative or technical information expressed in words in a text into visual form (e.g., a table or chart) and translate information expressed visually or mathematically (e.g., in an equation) into words."];
  "csp.RST.6-8.7" [label="Integrate quantitative or technical information expressed in words in a text with a version of that information expressed visually (e.g., in a flowchart, diagram, model, graph, or table)."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.8" [label="Assess the extent to which the reasoning and evidence in a text support the author's claim or a recommendation for solving a scientific or technical problem."];
  "csp.4.R.RS.8" [label="Distinguish among facts, reasoned judgment based on research findings and speculation in a text."];
  "csp.5.R.RS.9" [label="Compare and contrast findings presented in a text to those from other sources (including their own experiments), noting when the findings support or contradict previous explanations or accounts."];
  "csp.4.R.RS.9" [label="Compare and contrast the information gained from experiments, simulations, video, or multimedia sources with that gained from reading a text on the same topic."];
  "csp.6.R.RS.7" [label="Integrate and evaluate multiple sources of information presented in diverse formats and media (e.g., quantitative data, video, multimedia) in order to address a question or solve a problem."];
  "csp.11.13.8.8" [label="Evaluate the hypotheses, data, analysis, and conclusions in a science or technical text, verifying the data when possible and corroborating or challenging conclusions with other sources of information."];
  "csp.11.13.9.9" [label="Synthesize information from a range of sources (e.g., texts, experiments, simulations) into a coherent understanding of a process, phenomenon, or concept, resolving conflicting information when possible."];
  "csp.9.13.10.10" [label="By the end of grade 10, read and comprehend science/technical texts in the grades 9—10 text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "csp.RST.6-8.10" [label="By the end of grade 8, read and comprehend science/technical texts in the grades 6—8 text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "csp.11.13.10.10" [label="By the end of grade 12, read and comprehend science/technical texts in the grades 11—CCR text complexity band independently and proficiently."];
  "csp.W.9.5" [label="Develop and strengthen writing as needed by planning, revising, editing, rewriting, or trying a new approach, focusing on addressing what is most significant for a specific purpose and audience."];
  "csp.W.7.5" [label="With some guidance and support from peers and adults, develop and strengthen writing as needed by planning, revising, editing, rewriting, or trying a new approach, focusing on how well purpose and audience have been addressed."];
  "csp.W.9.6" [label="Use technology, including the Internet, to produce, publish, and update individual or shared writing products, taking advantage of technology's capacity to link to other information and to display information flexibly and dynamically."];
  "csp.6.W.WL.7" [label="Use technology, including the Internet, to produce and publish writing and present the relationships between information and ideas clearly and efficiently."];
  "csp.W.11.6" [label="Use technology, including the Internet, to produce, publish, and update individual or shared writing products in response to ongoing feedback, including new arguments or information."];
  "csp.W.9.7" [label="Conduct short as well as more sustained research projects to answer a question (including a self-generated question) or solve a problem; narrow or broaden the inquiry when appropriate; synthesize multiple sources on the subject, demonstrating understanding of the subject under investigation."];
  "csp.W.8.7" [label="Conduct short research projects to answer a question (including a self-generated question), drawing on several sources and generating additional related, focused questions that allow for multiple avenues of exploration."];
  "csp.3.l" [label="Gather relevant information from multiple authoritative print and digital sources, using advanced searches effectively; assess the usefulness of each source in answering the research question; integrate information into the text selectively to maintain the flow of ideas, avoiding plagiarism and following a standard format for citation."];
  "csp.W.7.8" [label="Gather relevant information from multiple print and digital sources, using search terms effectively; assess the credibility and accuracy of each source; and quote or paraphrase the data and conclusions of others while avoiding plagiarism and following a standard format for citation."];
  "csp.WHST.11-12.8" [label="Gather relevant information from multiple authoritative print and digital sources, using advanced searches effectively; assess the strengths and limitations of each source in terms of the specific task, purpose, and audience; integrate information into the text selectively to maintain the flow of ideas, avoiding plagiarism and over-reliance on any one source and following a standard format for citation."];
  "opensalt.8.RN1" [label="Student can explain the difference between rational and irrational numbers."];
  "opensalt.7.MD6" [label="Student understands that every quotient of integers (with a non-zero divisor) is a rational number."];
  "opensalt.8.RN2" [label="Student can explain that the real numbers include both rational and irrational numbers."];
  "opensalt.7.CAV4" [label="Student can determine the area of composite two-dimensional figures."];
  "opensalt.8.PT3" [label="Student can apply the Pythagorean Theorem to solve problems involving two-dimensional figures, such as determining the side length of a right triangle."];
  "opensalt.8.PT4" [label="Student can apply the Pythagorean Theorem to find the distance between two points on the coordinate plane."];
  "opensalt.8.PT5" [label="Student can apply the Pythagorean Theorem to solve problems involving three-dimensional figures."];
  "opensalt.7.CAV5" [label="Student can determine the surface area of prisms and right circular cylinders using nets."];
